False. The coordinate axes
$$
A=\mathbb R\times\{0\},\qquad B=\{0\}\times\mathbb R
$$
are both closed nowhere dense subsets of $\mathbb R^2$, but every $(x,y)$ is $(x,0)+(0,y)$, so
$$
A+B=\mathbb R^2,
$$
which is not meagre by the <Baire category theorem>.

